      <span style="background: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.12); color: #c084fc; border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.35); padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 14px;">STATUTORY CLEARANCE</span>
      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Statutory Interstate e-Way Bills, Regulatory Clearances &amp; 100% Marine Insurance for Things To Check Packers And Movers</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>When planning your move, verifying statutory transit paperwork and risk coverage is non-negotiable for peace of mind. Before finalizing a service provider, you must meticulously review the **list of things in home movers and packers** to ensure they adhere to legal and safety standards.</p>
<p>A reputable company will provide transparent documentation that protects your assets during the **shifting household things from one place to another vehicle** process. This involves more than just loading trucks; it requires strict compliance with national regulations to avoid fines or disputes.</p>

<p>The primary document you should scrutinize is the GST e-Way Bill. Under current tax laws, goods in transit exceeding certain value thresholds require this digital permit. Ensure the movers generate this bill accurately, reflecting the consignor, consignee, and vehicle details. Additionally, insist on an IBA-approved Lorry Receipt (LR) or Bilty.</p>
<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">This serves as the legal contract between you and the transporter, detailing the contents, weight, and terms of carriage.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>Without an IBA-compliant LR, your claim for damages may be invalid.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>When you **check all the documents movers** provide, verify that the LR number matches the e-Way bill and that your name is correctly listed as the owner.</span></li></ul>

<p>Equally critical is securing comprehensive 100% declared-value IRDAI marine transit insurance. Standard liability coverage is often insufficient for high-value items. True protection covers accidental collisions, fire, theft, and even unforeseen delays that might spoil perishables or sensitive electronics.</p>
<p>Ask for a policy endorsement that explicitly mentions "all risks" coverage up to the full declared value of your goods. Do not settle for basic statutory insurance unless you accept the significant financial risk.</p>

